              "C": "Use f106a25c73b44358 as the primary parallel reference: 128-by-128 tiles, single rolling bottom/right frontiers, and one persistent OpenMP team measured 10.95 ms, the best available result. Investigate tile shape, granularity, and a serial crossover appropriate to the fixed four-core ARM64 target. Compare tile-local versions of A's row fusion and B's prefix scans separately. Preserve wavefront ordering: tiles on one diagonal own distinct frontier ranges, and the barrier must publish both boundaries before the next diagonal. Retain sparse, deduplicated obstacle representation and thread-private scratch. Compare against the 256-tile program at 11.25 ms without attributing its difference solely to tile size, since parsing, indexing, and buffering also differ.",
